# Timeline: Snapshots

Spec: SnapshotsIndex
Purpose:
  Entry point for immutable system snapshots (SNAPSHOT-YYYY-MM-DD-NNN).
  Snapshots are state pointers to versioned system components at a point
  in time — NOT full file copies.

Owns: timeline/snapshots/

Structure:
  Snapshots are .sdd files with SNAPSHOT-YYYY-MM-DD-NNN IDs.
  Each snapshot references: constitution version, skills, architecture, decisions, knowledge.

Rules:
  [SNAPSHOT-01] Snapshots are immutable once created.
  [SNAPSHOT-02] New state → new snapshot, never modify existing.
  [SNAPSHOT-03] Tasks pin to a specific snapshot for reproducibility.

Navigation:
  Parent: @../INDEX.sdd
  SnapshotRecords: @../snapshots.sdd
  Changes: @../changes\INDEX.sdd
  Migrations: @../migrations\INDEX.sdd
  Evolution: @../evolution.sdd

State: +
